# rlsorens.msg - Director Sorensen, Amenities Office (Vault City), first regular of the Cesspit
# Plain ASCII only: the English Fallout 2 fonts have no umlauts or typographic quotes.

{100}{}{(A pale man in a citizen's jumpsuit freezes on the cellar stairs.) I'm not here. You didn't see me. I'm at a council hearing on public decency until midnight. Who are you?}
{101}{}{I need papers for this house.}
{102}{}{(Sorensen checks the stairs before he speaks.) Keep your voice down. What is it?}
{108}{}{Enjoy your evening, Director.}
{109}{}{Stairs?}

# Papers
{110}{}{Papers. (He licks his lips.) Five hundred, and I stamp a permit for a "boarding house with storage cellar." Nobody at the office reads past the first line. I should know. I wrote the form.}
{111}{}{[Barter] Here's $500. Make it official.}
{112}{}{Let's talk about something else.}
{113}{}{(He stamps it right there on the stairs, with a stamp he carries in his breast pocket.) Official. And now we both have something to lose.}
{114}{}{(Hanne takes the permit and pins it next to the door.) The cellar is yours now. I keep the house.}

# The gate guard (dark)
{120}{}{Lean on one of the gate guards for us. You sign their duty rosters.}
{121}{}{(Sorensen goes grey.) If I do that, you own me. (He does it anyway. The guard will warn you a week ahead of any raid, and Sorensen will never again be able to say no to you.)}

# Buying back the arrested
{130}{}{Buy our people out of the Corrections Center. ($}
{131}{}{)}
{132}{}{(Sorensen fills out a transfer form: "released to private employer for re-education".) They'll be back by morning. Don't make me do this twice.}

# Servant lease (tyrant route)
{140}{}{The Servant Allocation Center has people. Lease me one. ($50 a week)}
{141}{}{(He writes it up as "domestic assistance for a registered boarding house".) Fifty a week, paid to the city. She still belongs to Vault City. If there's ever a raid, she's a witness.}
{145}{}{Send the leased servants back.}
{146}{}{(Sorensen signs the return form without looking at it.) Returned. Nobody will ask where they were. Nobody ever does.}

# Look
{300}{}{A pale man in a citizen's jumpsuit who keeps looking at the stairs.}
{301}{}{Director Sorensen of the Amenities Office. By day he stamps permits. By night he was never here.}
